WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.619
The copper runs reach the management switches
in the end of row rack.

2
00:00:07.369 --> 00:00:12.425
This video covers how those switches reach the
management spines.

3
00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:20.225
We will look at the LC panel at RU
thirty-nine, the two trunk sizes, what each

4
00:00:20.225 --> 00:00:26.511
fiber pair carries, how to land the trunks,
and how the SPOCS racks connect.

5
00:00:30.661 --> 00:00:38.625
Every end of row rack has a one rack unit LC
panel at RU thirty-nine, for its management

6
00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:39.258
trunks.

7
00:00:40.658 --> 00:00:45.842
It has columns A to L, each with two
positions, in three rows.

8
00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:48.661
Row one is at the bottom.

9
00:00:50.011 --> 00:00:52.763
The trunk lands on the rear of the panel.

10
00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:56.031
Switch cords plug into the front.

11
00:00:56.781 --> 00:01:01.453
The switch cords are two-fiber LC duplex patch
cords.

12
00:01:02.803 --> 00:01:09.203
Each end of row rack connects to each of the
two management spines with one trunk.

13
00:01:09.953 --> 00:01:14.667
The management spine racks are 131 and 204.

14
00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:23.148
A standard end of row rack uses twelve-fiber
trunks.

15
00:01:23.898 --> 00:01:27.077
Twelve fibers is six duplex pairs.

16
00:01:28.427 --> 00:01:34.784
The spine one trunk uses positions A1 and A2,
in all three rows.

17
00:01:36.134 --> 00:01:42.598
The spine two trunk uses positions C5 and C6,
in all three rows.

18
00:01:43.948 --> 00:01:49.324
On the drawing, the duplex numbers count up
each column from the bottom.

19
00:01:50.074 --> 00:01:52.975
So duplex one is A1, row one.

20
00:01:54.325 --> 00:01:58.251
Duplex one carries the management leaf uplink.

21
00:01:59.001 --> 00:02:02.414
Duplex two carries the TROSS leaf uplink.

22
00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:05.084
Three to six are spares.

23
00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:09.802
The cutsheet gives the exact position for each
cord.

24
00:02:13.952 --> 00:02:24.782
The six end of row racks with BMS, 611, 613,
1411, 1413, 2211 and 2213, use

25
00:02:24.782 --> 00:02:29.547
twenty-four-fiber trunks instead.

26
00:02:30.297 --> 00:02:32.643
That is twelve duplex pairs.

27
00:02:33.993 --> 00:02:39.497
Their spine one trunk uses A1 through B4, rows
one to three.

28
00:02:40.247 --> 00:02:44.407
Their spine two trunk uses C5 through D8.

29
00:02:45.757 --> 00:02:51.731
Duplex one and two are the same as before:
management leaf and TROSS leaf.

30
00:02:53.081 --> 00:02:58.201
Duplex three carries the FB0 BMS switch
uplink.

31
00:02:58.951 --> 00:03:03.303
That is the building management system, lesson
fourteen.

32
00:03:04.653 --> 00:03:11.597
Duplex four to nine are for the SPOCS racks'
management uplinks, and ten to twelve are

33
00:03:11.597 --> 00:03:12.162
spares.

34
00:03:13.512 --> 00:03:17.523
One drawing says these racks use twelve-fiber
trunks.

35
00:03:18.273 --> 00:03:24.737
The guide corrected it to twenty-four, based
on the patching drawing and the patch data.

36
00:03:25.487 --> 00:03:31.076
If you see a twelve-fiber trunk headed for one
of these racks, stop and ask.

37
00:03:35.226 --> 00:03:38.511
Here are the steps for landing management
trunks.

38
00:03:39.511 --> 00:03:41.837
First, confirm the rack type.

39
00:03:42.587 --> 00:03:46.064
BMS racks get twenty-four fiber trunks.

40
00:03:46.814 --> 00:03:48.883
All the others get twelve.

41
00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:57.307
On the rear, land the spine one trunk and the
spine two trunk on their positions, in rows

42
00:03:57.307 --> 00:03:58.340
one to three.

43
00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:08.185
On the front, plug in the switch cords: duplex
one for the management leaf, two for the TROSS

44
00:04:08.185 --> 00:04:12.661
leaf, and on BMS racks, three for the FB0
switch.

45
00:04:14.011 --> 00:04:16.763
Store trunk slack on top of the rack.

46
00:04:17.513 --> 00:04:22.270
Wrap-around labels on the trunks, flag labels
on the cords.

47
00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:28.228
At the management spine rack, each trunk lands
on a panel.

48
00:04:28.978 --> 00:04:38.124
From the panel front, a breakout harness joins
four LC legs into one MPO-8 plug at the spine

49
00:04:38.124 --> 00:04:38.621
port.

50
00:04:39.971 --> 00:04:46.865
And that final patching at the spine rack must
be done before the rack is turned up, meaning

51
00:04:46.865 --> 00:04:48.888
powered and brought online.

52
00:04:53.038 --> 00:04:56.729
The SPOCS racks need management connections
too.

53
00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:06.725
Each SPOCS rack has two pre-installed
management switches near the top, called mgmt1

54
00:05:06.725 --> 00:05:07.825
and mgmt2.

55
00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:18.306
mgmt1 connects to the BMS end of row rack at
spot eleven, in its pod's BMS row.

56
00:05:19.656 --> 00:05:26.248
Mgmt two connects to the BMS end of row rack
at spot thirteen.

57
00:05:27.598 --> 00:05:31.523
Each uplink is a long two-fiber LC cord.

58
00:05:32.273 --> 00:05:39.302
It runs straight to the front of that rack's
RU thirty-nine panel, into a position whose

59
00:05:39.302 --> 00:05:42.577
rear carries the twenty-four fiber trunk.

60
00:05:43.327 --> 00:05:45.695
The cutsheet gives the position.

61
00:05:47.045 --> 00:05:52.507
From there, the twenty-four fiber trunks carry
them to the management spines.

62
00:05:53.257 --> 00:05:57.246
Each switch has two uplinks, one toward each
spine.

63
00:05:58.596 --> 00:06:06.258
One open question: the table reserves six
positions for SPOCS uplinks on each trunk, but

64
00:06:06.258 --> 00:06:09.305
the description works out to three.

65
00:06:10.055 --> 00:06:15.794
Use the cutsheet's exact positions, and ask
your lead if they do not match.

66
00:06:19.944 --> 00:06:27.622
In lesson thirteen of the course, practice
finding positions on the LC panel and routing

67
00:06:27.622 --> 00:06:29.629
SPOCS management cords.

